{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-095", "category": "formats_compile_faq", "context_hash": "50ced0e82f629baad16464fe1d3ee217a4ab28863f2742e77a7d437629f569e1", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Mesh module questions|paragraph|What should I do when the 2D unstructured algorithm fails?#2", "msgid": "If everything fails file a bug report with the version of your operating\nsystem and the full geometry.", "msgid_sha256": "fa2a2ce2969ce95480535f2b6808572aa8b669c5c8cfa234f716bbb3e2e0e0a4", "node": "Mesh module questions", "protected_hash": "4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945", "protected_values": [], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "032e56e0196791760e7fb4648c260c1d84e3f2211dcde9f93405fd9ab0497280", "semantic_key": "What should I do when the 2D unstructured algorithm fails?#2", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "3e7ea71c82a0f2a612943a39b88ff539d4605b5ceff71dcdf8bf5c5b7cbd3864", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Mesh module questions", "subcategory": "faq", "unit_id": "6e6a2098e9b4112c3f35b9adef473e46cf4920af61ec18dbb4963c55e78d0fc0"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-096", "category": "formats_compile_faq", "context_hash": "91721f2bba36ae8802fd7639c3a4d82cf38d578621678c95f952c45fe06a4c4b", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|General questions|item|The graphics display very slowly.", "msgid": "The graphics display very slowly.", "msgid_sha256": "14871805bca02e71ae032c3fd7c6e55afdfee93d92bdc52469816f5a08c4aacc", "node": "General questions", "protected_hash": "4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945", "protected_values": [], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "item", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "04a9c1c9c8be7ec986229b1a9da8ed49cc940e21337ccb127d48e9ae187a2583", "semantic_key": "The graphics display very slowly.", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "ec70c54f97a7d8e22c9438f0eb7f30f7e8e71042d732612fa3533e59b1ca9ca1", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::General questions", "subcategory": "faq", "unit_id": "a20ace23fc627a19a225b87cbc7f54c90a42d8d8a3fe46de210212f91a68825d"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-097", "category": "formats_compile_faq", "context_hash": "2b68cc4226b406796cbad7db0c249f9ac26c46214199e6d611731e43dd70ad15", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Mesh module questions|paragraph|How can I remove mesh nodes for geometrical construction points (centers of spheres, etc.) from output mesh file?", "msgid": "By default Gmsh saves all the geometrical entities and their associated\nmesh. In particular, since each geometry point is meshed with a point\nelement, defined by a mesh node, the output file will contain one 0-D\nmesh element and one mesh node for each geometry point. To remove such\nelements/nodes from the mesh, simply define physical groups for the\nentities you want to save (see previous question).", "msgid_sha256": "c4131e0a2c9da83242d82decde08d6971927dda06c35cde5565c8711f68dbdd9", "node": "Mesh module questions", "protected_hash": "a37bbbb0764cc5bf8d8c251cb1c95e3d2e142934792916ccb362ceb5902d9f0b", "protected_values": ["0"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "04d09e1448135fd611cc6600fd62a6617bb5eb4ec6aed5f6615178c33c1630ce", "semantic_key": "How can I remove mesh nodes for geometrical construction points (centers of spheres, etc.) from output mesh file?", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "171d0d7a570fd8296a9c79197ddbe239e938078f26ad5bb7227c3794cbe357af", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Mesh module questions", "subcategory": "faq", "unit_id": "a6d7cb3aed1bfe17f4df590cf030c883fc509fd1bc18a519e7d27130d6d6766c"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-098", "category": "formats_compile_faq", "context_hash": "368238049bdc4b9536de1d6d4b46202ecb6a7ae60d55fface15591a7ce9b236a", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Geometry module questions|paragraph|Gmsh is very slow when I use many transformations (Translate, Rotate, Symmetry, Extrude, etc.) with the built-in CAD kernel. What's wrong?", "msgid": "The default behavior of Gmsh is to check and suppress all duplicate\nentities (points, curves and surfaces) each time a transformation\ncommand is issued with the built-in CAD kernel. This can slow down\nthings a lot if many transformations are performed. There are two\nsolutions to this problem:", "msgid_sha256": "8af10f661542b2ec69e3af9f3bebe6b068f8e92fc30a56c9d9ede7fb57816d1c", "node": "Geometry module questions", "protected_hash": "4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945", "protected_values": [], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "071ed1ad09a9f918ed9589ba883e80388643f30b110253bf44bdbc0f91b6890f", "semantic_key": "Gmsh is very slow when I use many transformations (Translate, Rotate, Symmetry, Extrude, etc.) with the built-in CAD kernel. What's wrong?", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "33687159b39347fd8b52242c8378ef61b0424e3a2b6cc863b6a9b3950461ab4a", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Geometry module questions", "subcategory": "faq", "unit_id": "a145c0f18a2b690c9788424fe776f5070b7afd6a9b77ab1ef8dd359d90d50dc9"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-099", "category": "formats_compile_faq", "context_hash": "c9a876ee2a5c20bea3b465fa0ffbb6dd733203c5671337954939d4bd51231a50", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Post-processing module questions|item|How can I see ``inside'' a complicated post-processing view?", "msgid": "How can I see ``inside'' a complicated post-processing view?", "msgid_sha256": "4891ece5b04a28c41f066d15d81897f73cae3b054be5d2293842fc9a0eb831a6", "node": "Post-processing module questions", "protected_hash": "4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945", "protected_values": [], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "item", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "08644e37477d9e1bd225971e09b0853a784cd14cd23b8bc18790fd8a345d8887", "semantic_key": "How can I see ``inside'' a complicated post-processing view?", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "7a1783fa3e4714d0fa7a36f60461f54a07ccfe776a2f1f1300859349e7404a16", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Post-processing module questions", "subcategory": "faq", "unit_id": "719be075454dda82cdef37dd9f2786a02681732a8782aa8cfdd199ecf9f7d42c"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-100", "category": "formats_compile_faq", "context_hash": "186a5141cbfc8e18bab00220dcfb95b4b0301914ed562d4a3990f9d62f0c0018", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Mesh module questions|paragraph|Can I import an existing surface mesh in Gmsh and use it to build a 3D mesh?", "msgid": "Yes, you can import a surface mesh in any one of the supported mesh file\nformats, define a volume, and mesh it. For an example see\n@url{@value{GITLAB-PREFIX}/examples/simple_geo/sphere-discrete.geo,examples/simple_geo/sphere-discrete.geo}.", "msgid_sha256": "2ed887ddeba50ee9aae653bf80c1ef75c094d99350ae108a02bf28df5bfc925f", "node": "Mesh module questions", "protected_hash": "af49f777c8d763e5dce79a771bfba5c9673a05a67f1aab4b6e0b3864a3350d62", "protected_values": ["@url{@value{GITLAB-PREFIX}/examples/simple_geo/sphere-discrete.geo,", "}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "08bc6ce22213a04626495d9235f9acd2f0ace86caffb1b39b97aa9ed5a9924f4", "semantic_key": "Can I import an existing surface mesh in Gmsh and use it to build a 3D mesh?", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "4e3e82464f2fc81aadec5627373a93fd2e8ea7357a30c78e2f1b76b5eff32455", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Mesh module questions", "subcategory": "faq", "unit_id": "40df85153280de8eaa5450fadb0ca2e0b8530064d2ff84d322b0184ad50e072b"}
